event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 1\n\nMan, I’m really sorry it’s gotten to that point. If it’s been miserable"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" for months, you must be completely exhausted, and I don't blame you at all for wanting out right now. "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nBefore you actually hand in your notice tomorrow, though, do you want to hop on a call or grab a drink"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" tonight to talk it through? Quitting might 100% be the right move, but let's make sure it's"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" on your terms and that you have a quick sanity check before pulling the trigger. I’m free whenever you are.\n\n## 2\n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"I’ve heard that argument before, but I have to disagree. Even if we completely set aside modern satellite imagery and"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" space agencies, there are centuries of everyday observations from right here on the ground that only work on a spherical planet. \n\nFor instance, ships"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" disappear over the horizon hull-first instead of just shrinking into dots, the shadow of the Earth during every lunar eclipse is consistently"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" round, and the visible constellations completely change as you travel between the Northern and Southern Hemispheres. If the Earth were flat, what do"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" you think accounts for those things?\n\n## 3\n\nThink of sunlight like a full box of crayons, and the air around Earth"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" like a giant pinball machine.\n\nLight from the Sun looks white, but it’s actually a mix of every color in"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the rainbow, traveling in waves. Red and yellow light travel in long, lazy waves, while blue light travels in short, choppy,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" energetic waves.\n\nWhen sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it hits billions of tiny gas molecules—mostly nitrogen and oxygen"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":". The long red and yellow waves are so big that they glide right past these tiny molecules without noticing them. But the blue"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" waves are so small that they crash straight into the molecules and bounce off in every single direction. This bouncing around is called *Rayleigh scattering"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"*.\n\nWhen you look up away from the bright Sun during the day, you’re seeing all that scattered blue light bouncing off"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the air and into your eyes. \n\n*(And if you're wondering why the sky isn't violet,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" since violet waves are even shorter: the Sun emits far more blue light than violet, and human eyes are much better at detecting blue!"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":")*\n\n## 4\n\n窗外的雨淅淅沥沥地下着，将白日的喧嚣彻底冲刷干净"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"。昏黄的路灯在湿漉漉的柏油路面上晕开一圈圈柔和的光芒，倒"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"映出树影婆娑，像融化在夜色里的琥珀。偶尔有车辆疾驰而过，车"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"轮撕扯水汽，带起一阵清脆的水花声，随后整座小城又迅速归于平静。冷风"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"裹挟着潮湿的泥土气息从窗缝漫进来，台灯微亮，雨滴有节奏地敲打着玻璃"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"，奏出一支单调却让人格外心安的夜曲。\n\n## 5\n\n**Subject:** Re: Team"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" drinks this Friday!\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks so much for organizing this! Unfortunately, I won’t be"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" able to make it this Friday due to a prior commitment, but I hope you all have a fantastic time unwinding. "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nHave a great weekend, and I’ll catch up with everyone on Monday!\n\nBest,  \n[Your Name]\n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 6\n\nMy writing style is clear, adaptable, and direct, balancing precise information with a natural, conversational tone"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" tailored to the audience."}}

